  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\int \\frac{\\sin x}{\\sin (x-\\alpha)} d x=A x+B \\log \\sin (x-\\alpha)+C$, then value of $(A, B)$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$(\\sin \\alpha, \\cos \\alpha)$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$(\\cos \\alpha, \\sin \\alpha)$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$(-\\sin \\alpha, \\cos \\alpha)$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$(-\\cos \\alpha, \\sin \\alpha)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Put $x-\\alpha=t$\n$\\Rightarrow \\int \\frac{\\sin (\\alpha+t)}{\\sin t} d t=\\sin \\alpha \\int \\cot t d t+\\cos \\alpha \\int d t$\n$=\\cos \\alpha(x-\\alpha)+\\sin \\alpha \\ln |\\sin t|+c$\n$A=\\cos \\alpha, B=\\sin \\alpha$"
  }
}